# application/vnd.fafm+yaml — mcp-trinity project memory
# Real, dogfooded memory about this repo's own build — not a static example.
# This file itself is one of the three sources the server exposes:
# `remember` / `recall` read and write it, and the demo proves a fact
# survives a full server-process restart (then restores this file exactly).
version: "1.1"
profile: "knowledge"
namepoint: "@mcp-trinity:public"
created: "2026-08-12T00:00:00Z"
last_etched: "2026-08-12T00:00:00Z"
retention: "forever"

index:
  - "mcp-trinity — an MCP server that publishes a project's context, memory & identity"
  - "context concern leads with AGENTS.md (text/markdown); memory & identity use .fafm/.fafa as worked examples"
  - "two exposure surfaces: Server Card _meta block + self-published ai-catalog.json"

memory:
  facts:
    - text: "The context concern points at AGENTS.md — the de-facto standard for agent instructions. read_agents_md serves it whole or one section at a time, so a client pulls '## Test' without spending its context window on the whole file. Memory and identity have no de-facto standard, so the reference uses .fafm and .fafa as one instantiation each."
      id: "mcp-trinity-scope"
      type: "reference"
      priority: "high"
      tags: ["scope", "agents-md"]
      source: "README.md"
      verification_status: "verified"

    - text: "Both exposure mechanisms — the Server Card _meta block and a self-published ai-catalog.json — already exist in the MCP ecosystem. This server wires all three concerns through them, from one set of source files, with a CI check (catalog:check) that fails if the two surfaces drift apart."
      id: "mechanisms-already-proven"
      type: "reference"
      priority: "high"
      tags: ["mcp", "server-card", "ai-catalog"]
      links: ["mcp-trinity-scope"]
      source: "docs/MECHANISMS.md"
      verification_status: "verified"

    - text: "Distribution: a published npm package (bin `mcp-trinity`, dual transport). The three source files (AGENTS.md, project.fafm, .well-known/fafa) ship with the package so it is a working discovery target on install. MCP_TRINITY_ROOT points it at a real project."
      id: "distribution-model"
      type: "reference"
      priority: "standard"
      tags: ["distribution", "mit", "npm"]
      source: "README.md"
      verification_status: "verified"
  sessions: []
  preferences: {}
  custom: {}
